# TinyML-Based Hybrid Calibration Framework for Soil Nutrient Monitoring in Precision Farming

## Project Overview

This project presents a TinyML-based soil nutrient monitoring system for precision farming. The system uses an Arduino Uno (ATmega328), NPK sensor, soil moisture sensor, and temperature sensor to collect soil parameters.

Machine learning techniques are used for sensor data analysis and hybrid calibration to improve the estimation of soil nutrient values.

## Hardware

- Arduino Uno (ATmega328)
- NPK Sensor
- Soil Moisture Sensor
- Temperature Sensor

## Technologies Used

- Arduino IDE
- Python
- Jupyter Notebook
- Machine Learning
- TinyML

## Project Objectives

- Monitor soil nutrient parameters in real time
- Collect and process soil sensor data
- Apply sensor calibration techniques
- Develop a lightweight machine learning model suitable for edge deployment
- Improve soil nutrient estimation for precision agriculture

## Team

Team Size: 3

## Project Status

Prototype developed and tested.
